      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: why was it disabled in worlds too then? And why remove the *entire* feature because some people would leave it on by mistake? And why did this just happen to be removed in the Unity 2017 update, with no mention of it in the changelog at all?\n\nEspecially in worlds, the doppler effect makes sound FX a lot better. It makes no sense for it to be intentionally removed. This is yet another removed feature to be added to the casualties. This world used it to great effect: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l37yS0RUkgk\n\nIf you're really concerned about the default doppler settings not being newbie-friendly, then why not implement a very simple editor script into the SDK to automatically set it to 0 when adding an audio source?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
